<h2 id="what-are-status-ads">What are WhatsApp Status ads?</h2>
<p>Status ads are paid ads that appear in WhatsApp's <strong>Updates tab</strong>, mixed in between people's regular Status updates. They look like a Status post with a label showing it is sponsored. A user can skip it, or tap through to start a chat with the business or visit a website.</p>

<p>Three things to know:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>No ads in personal chats.</strong> Meta says ads, promotions and subscriptions appear only in the Updates tab, separate from personal chats and calls. Chats remain end-to-end encrypted.</li>
    <li><strong>They sit next to Promoted Channels.</strong> In the same tab, businesses can also pay to promote their WhatsApp Channel in the channels directory. That builds followers; a Status ad aims at a conversation or a click.</li>
    <li><strong>They start conversations.</strong> Meta's stated purpose is to help people find a new business and easily start a conversation about the product or service shown in the ad.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="availability-india">Are WhatsApp Status ads available in India?</h2>
<p>Yes. In <a href="https://www.socialsamosa.com/industry-updates/whatsapp-new-ad-features-businesses-10470657" target="_blank" rel="noopener">September 2025, Meta announced</a> that Indian businesses could add WhatsApp placements to campaigns in Meta Ads Manager, alongside Facebook and Instagram. Maruti Suzuki, Air India and Flipkart were named as early Status advertisers. Meta has since <a href="https://betanews.com/article/whatsapp-rolls-out-promoted-channels-and-ads-in-status-globally/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rolled out Status ads and Promoted Channels globally</a>.</p>

<p>The rollout to advertiser accounts has been gradual. If you do not see the WhatsApp Status placement in your Ads Manager yet, it may not have reached your account.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-set-up">How to set up a WhatsApp Status ad</h2>
<p>According to <a href="https://faq.whatsapp.com/1741293046527876" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp's help centre</a>, Status ads are created in Meta Ads Manager using the WhatsApp Status placement. The usual steps:</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Connect your WhatsApp Business account</strong> to your Facebook Page or Meta Business account, so ads can open a chat with your business number.</li>
    <li><strong>Create a campaign</strong> in Meta Ads Manager and choose an objective that fits your goal—for example, more messages or more website traffic.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose the destination:</strong> a WhatsApp chat with your business, or your website or landing page.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick placements.</strong> Select manual placements and turn on <em>WhatsApp Status</em>. Some advertisers report that Status has to run together with other Stories placements, such as Instagram Stories; follow what your Ads Manager allows.</li>
    <li><strong>Upload a vertical creative.</strong> Status is full-screen and vertical, like Stories, so use a 9:16 image or short video with the main message in the first second.</li>
    <li><strong>Set budget and audience,</strong> then publish and watch the first few days closely.</li>
</ol>
<p>The WhatsApp Business app also has its own option to create ads in Status for simpler, small-budget campaigns.</p>

<h2 id="cost">How much do WhatsApp Status ads cost in India?</h2>
<p>There is <strong>no fixed price</strong>. Status ads run in Meta's normal ad auction, like Facebook and Instagram ads, so the cost depends on your audience, competition, budget, creative quality and season. Meta does not publish official rates for the placement. Estimates on agency and vendor blogs vary widely, so treat any number you see online as indicative only.</p>

<p>The more useful number is your own: <strong>cost per qualified lead</strong>. A cheap click that never replies is not cheap. Start with a small daily budget you are comfortable testing for one to two weeks, then judge results by how many chats became real enquiries. Taxes apply to ad spend in India, so include them in your budget. Our <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-cost-india">guide to judging ad cost by qualified leads</a> explains the same method for another channel.</p>

<h2 id="targeting-privacy">Targeting and privacy: what Meta can and cannot use</h2>
<p>Status ads use a deliberately limited set of signals compared with Facebook and Instagram. Meta says targeting can draw on basic information such as country or city, device language, the channels a person follows and how they interact with ads in the Updates tab. Personal messages are not used.</p>
<p>Users can block or hide ads from a specific business directly in the app. That makes creative quality important: an irrelevant or pushy ad can be hidden quickly. In the European region, users can pay to remove ads from Status and Channels; this does not affect Indian users.</p>

<h2 id="who-should-use">Which businesses should test Status ads?</h2>
<p>Status ads suit businesses whose customers prefer to ask questions on WhatsApp before buying:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Local services:</strong> clinics, salons, coaching classes, repair and home services.</li>
    <li><strong>Real estate:</strong> project launches and site-visit bookings, where a quick chat is the natural next step.</li>
    <li><strong>Retail and D2C brands:</strong> offers, new arrivals and festive sales.</li>
    <li><strong>Events and education:</strong> admissions, workshops and webinars with a deadline.</li>
</ul>
<p>They are a weaker fit for complex B2B sales with long decision cycles, where LinkedIn or search ads usually reach decision-makers better. A Status ad is an interruption, not a search, so it works best for offers people did not know they wanted until they saw them.</p>

<h2 id="tips">Tips for a successful first campaign</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Be ready to reply fast.</strong> A Status ad that opens a chat is only as good as your response time. Set up a greeting message and quick replies, or use <a href="/blog/top-benefits-whatsapp-automation-lead-follow-up">WhatsApp automation for lead follow-up</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Make one clear offer.</strong> "Free consultation this week" works better than a list of services.</li>
    <li><strong>Design for sound off and small screens.</strong> Use large text, a clear face or product, and your brand in the first second.</li>
    <li><strong>Test two or three creatives,</strong> then keep the one that produces the most qualified chats, not just the most taps.</li>
    <li><strong>Track every lead.</strong> Tag WhatsApp enquiries by source so you can compare Status ads with Instagram, Facebook and Google.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The practical takeaway</h2>
<p>WhatsApp Status ads give Indian businesses a new way to reach customers inside the app they use most, with a direct path to a conversation. They are worth a small, measured test if your customers already like to enquire on WhatsApp and your team can reply quickly. Judge them by qualified leads, not cheap clicks.</p>

